          "content": "BRIEF — Studio · mobile 1",
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "MJ8q7",
          "name": "Body",
          "fill": "$graphite",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "kit-version-source: 0.3.0 · brief-schema: 1 · updated: 2026-09-27\nTHE DESIGN WE WANT, compared against the app. In code (#110–#117, #123–#128): the piece in the panel, one status chip, notices resolved together, Field and readable text, amber for selection only (K6), the expert's memory above the conversation (UI-4), a quiet \"+\" (UI-11), the cost first in Materials (UI-16), History and Notices without nested cards, the tray on one line. Open decisions are in CODE_CHANGES §7. Icons in this file are Pencil's (no fill weight, no hammer): the code's icons win. Screens named \"capture\" are the app as it is and stay that way.\n1. PURPOSE\nThe furniture is the interface (D38): the 3D is never covered, and every action says whether it happens now or goes to the expert.\n2. ENTRY POINTS\nAfter Capture (flows/capture.pen), or an example from Home.\n3. SCREENS (columns are areas; a column's states stack below it)\n- Conversation / Default — one-row scene bar with \"Armado\" labeled (UI-5); \"+\" is a quiet ghost next to settings (UI-11); on a phone the header is icons with accessible names (K4 narrowed to content, decided 2026-09-28)\n- Piece / Selected — the piece replaces the panel, like Notices and History already do; the 3D stays whole (B-2, the rule in Studio.tsx:146)\n- Conversation / Thinking\n- Conversation / Proposal pending — one status chip over the 3D (UI-5); the instant fix is the primary action; \"Aplicar así, bajo mi riesgo\" is a visible secondary button (UI-6, UI-17)\n- Notices / Critical — the same radio ways and one \"Resolver 1\" as Several (decided 2026-09-28: one grammar, UI-6, UI-15); no card inside a card (UI-2)\n- Conversation / Tray — the tray is one line, the chat stays readable (UI-14)\n- Notices / Several, after choosing — nothing comes pre-checked; each notice picks its way; one \"Resolver N\" applies the ⚡ ones now (one version) and sends the rest to the expert in one request (UI-15)\n- Materials / Expert working in the background — nothing is disabled; a global indicator with the real stage and Cancel sits over the 3D (UI-15)\n- Materials / Expert answered — a count on Conversación and \"Resuelto: …\" over the 3D (UI-18)\n- Materials screens show the estimated cost before the review; the list stays behind it (UI-16, D30 holds). \"~$3,165\" is from the v2 capture (300 mm deep)\n4. BUSINESS RULES\nUnchanged: D4, D30, D34, D36, D37.\n5. COPY SOURCE\nsrc/ui/** and the simulated expert. The ⚡ fix and group resolve: src/ui/chat/ProposalFix.tsx (\"Aplicar con un apoyo al centro\") and src/ui/studio/NoticePanel.tsx (\"Resolver 2\", \"al instante\", \"al experto\", \"Resuelto: …\").\n6. STATES NOT DRAWN\nNone: every state in code is drawn or captured. The ⋯ menu was dropped — UI-11 chose a quiet \"+\" instead.\n7. OPEN FINDINGS\nUI-1, UI-2, UI-3, UI-5, UI-6, UI-11, UI-14, UI-15, UI-16, UI-17, UI-18, B-2\n8. HISTORY\n→ LOG frame, below.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
