    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "j2lsX",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1310,
      "name": "BRIEF — Studio · mobile 2",
      "clip": true,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 1180,
      "fill": "$paper",
      "cornerRadius": "$radius-2xl",
      "stroke": "$line",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 10,
      "padding": 32,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "I9FXAk",
          "name": "Heading",
          "fill": "$graphite",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "BRIEF — Studio · mobile 2",
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "NWevI",
          "name": "Body",
          "fill": "$graphite",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "kit-version-source: 0.3.0 · brief-schema: 1 · updated: 2026-09-27\nTHE DESIGN WE WANT, compared against the app. In code (#110–#117, #123–#128): the piece in the panel, one status chip, notices resolved together, Field and readable text, amber for selection only (K6), the expert's memory above the conversation (UI-4), a quiet \"+\" (UI-11), the cost first in Materials (UI-16), History and Notices without nested cards, the tray on one line. Open decisions are in CODE_CHANGES §7. Icons in this file are Pencil's (no fill weight, no hammer): the code's icons win. Screens named \"capture\" are the app as it is and stay that way.\n1. PURPOSE\nThe rest of the Studio's sections in the same grammar as band 1.\n2. ENTRY POINTS\nTap a piece, \"Editar a mano\"; the Mueble and Materiales tabs; the version button in the header.\n3. SCREENS (columns are areas; a column's states stack below it)\n- Piece / Editing by hand — the edit form lives in the piece sheet, the 3D stays whole (B-2); move buttons follow the piece's axis (PieceEditor.tsx MOVE)\n- Piece / Hidden, show all — \"Ocultar\" in the piece sheet hides it; while any piece is hidden the status chip says \"1 pieza oculta\" with \"Mostrar todo\", ahead of a proposal (decided 2026-09-28, #131)\n- History keeps \"Bitácora: qué hizo el experto\" under the list, and \"Qué cambió\" is a flat line (decided 2026-09-28)\n- Furniture / Plan sheet — the tab is the plan sheet only; the kind is one compact line; the expert's memory is no longer here (UI-4)\n- Materials / Fix before buying — cost first (UI-16), then the verdict and the checks; sentence-case labels (UI-2)\n- Notices / Nothing pending, Furniture / No plan sheet, Materials / Sheets to buy and Sheet layout: captures of the app, unchanged\n- History / Two versions — a flat timeline, no card inside a card; \"Volver a esta\" is a visible button (UI-17 family)\n- Captures of the app for the states that stay as they are: the expert asks with options, the expert failed with \"Reintentar\", a hand edit rejected with its alternatives, the plan sheet with changes, a kind change that needs a redo, reviewing, not viable with \"Ver la lista de todos modos\", cut settings, editing a price, viewing an old version, the expert's settings, unlocking saved keys, and confirming \"Nuevo diseño\"\n- Conversation / Expert's memory, open — the memory folds above the conversation: closed it is one line with a count; open it holds the requirements, the design decisions and the add-note field (UI-4, src/ui/chat/Memory.tsx)\nCaptures retaken 2026-09-28 with #131 (camera, shadows, hide) and #132 (no nested cards, flat \"Qué cambió\", suggestions give way to the tray)\n4. BUSINESS RULES\nHand edits apply at once and are checked like any change; the plan applies on \"Aplicar\" (D34). The list stays behind the review (D30).\n5. COPY SOURCE\nsrc/ui/studio/{PieceEditor,FurniturePanel,PlanSheet,Materials,Verdict,HistoryPanel}.tsx; src/ui/chat/Memory.tsx; src/ui/studio/{PieceSheet,Studio}.tsx for \"Ocultar\" and the hidden chip; verdict text from the simulated expert. \"~$3,165\" from the v2 capture.\n6. STATES NOT DRAWN\nSeveral pieces hidden: the same chip, \"N piezas ocultas\".\n7. OPEN FINDINGS\nUI-2, UI-16, UI-17, B-2\n8. HISTORY\n→ LOG frame, below.\nPROPOSALS 2026-09-28 (not in code yet): screens named above; open questions live in the playground log and the PR.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
