        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "hZMSC",
          "name": "Body",
          "fill": "$graphite",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "kit-version-source: 0.3.0 · brief-schema: 1 · updated: 2026-09-27\nTHE DESIGN WE WANT, compared against the app. In code (#110–#117, #123–#128): the piece in the panel, one status chip, notices resolved together, Field and readable text, amber for selection only (K6), the expert's memory above the conversation (UI-4), a quiet \"+\" (UI-11), the cost first in Materials (UI-16), History and Notices without nested cards, the tray on one line. Open decisions are in CODE_CHANGES §7. Icons in this file are Pencil's (no fill weight, no hammer): the code's icons win. Screens named \"capture\" are the app as it is and stay that way.\n1. PURPOSE\nThe same Studio at a desk (D38: equal weight): 3D on the left, a 420 px panel on the right.\n2. ENTRY POINTS\nSame as the mobile bands.\n3. SCREENS (columns are areas; a column's states stack below it)\n- Conversation / Default — labels on everything: \"Armado\", \"Cotas\", \"Simulado\", \"Nuevo diseño\" as a ghost (UI-11, Doña Carmen)\n- Piece / Selected, editing — the piece takes the panel, same pattern as mobile; editing is open because there is room (B-2); the fields carry mm only, no cm line (decided 2026-09-28); \"Ocultar\" next to the close button\n- Conversation / Proposal pending — status chip over the 3D; ⚡ fix as the primary action; \"bajo mi riesgo\" a visible secondary (UI-6, UI-17)\n- Notices / Several, after choosing — one \"Resolver 2\" (UI-15)\n- Notices / Nothing pending, Furniture / No plan sheet, Materials / Sheets to buy and Sheet layout: captures of the app\n- Settings / The expert, and New design confirm: captures of the app\n- Materials / Cost first, expert working — cost and sheets without waiting, the expert working in the background with the global indicator (UI-15, UI-16)\n4. BUSINESS RULES\nDesktop ≥ 768 px (Studio.tsx useDesktop). D30, D34, D36, D37 unchanged.\n5. COPY SOURCE\nSame as the mobile bands, plus the sheet rows from Materials.tsx.\n6. STATES NOT DRAWN\nHidden pieces on desktop: the same chip as mobile. The review gate's check list and the sheet diagrams stay as the app draws them (decided 2026-09-28): see the Materials captures.\nThe rest of the states on desktop are the mobile ones in the side panel; history and the plan sheet are the same, wider.\nLIFT, later: the piece sheet leaves half the desktop panel empty — room for the piece's cut-list line and its joints drawn.\n7. OPEN FINDINGS\nUI-6, UI-11, UI-15, UI-16, UI-17, B-2\n8. HISTORY\n→ LOG frame, below.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "frame",
